    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328-a1">

                <pb facs="0769" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg721"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 17, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned representatives, having this day met, unanimously adopted the
                    following resolution:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved,</hi> That in consequence of the arrival in this
                    harbor of Japanese steamers carrying large numbers of troops, the naval and
                    military officers of the respective forces be requested to take, as soon as
                    possible, such measures as are necessary to prevent the landing of armed
                    Japanese along the water front of Yokohama.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. ROCHES.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HARRY S. PARKES.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CTE. DE LA TOUR.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. VON BRANDT.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. DE GRAEFF VON POLSBROECK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
